  "kind": "promo",
  "title": "The Day After the Target",
  "subtitle": "Dr Joost Nwosu, Postdoctoral Fellow",
  "summary": "Dr Joost Nwosu, Postdoctoral Fellow in the School of Continuous Improvement, introduces in his own words the question his research keeps returning to: what becomes of a target once it has been met. Three of his outputs supply the answers so far, a community choir that retires a song once its tuner log is satisfied, a school sausage sizzle whose shire lowers the limit it has just come in under, and a junior swim club where a personal best becomes the floor for every swim after it. The profile closes on the funding, outputs and citations that make him the best-funded researcher in his School.",
  "topic": "a promo profile of Dr Joost Nwosu, the best-funded researcher in the School of Continuous Improvement, in his own voice: a postdoctoral fellow who studies what happens to a target once it is met, whether it is retired, made quietly tougher or kept on as a floor, through a choir's tuner log, a sausage sizzle's notification ceiling and a junior swim club's personal-best ledger",
